  "description": "For an almost effortless way to a more interesting cheese platter, marinate fresh goat cheese in olive oil with herbs and spices. We add fennel seed, lemon zest, bay leaves, and more for a well-rounded infusion of flavor.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr 10 min to 2 days 10 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: 2 teaspoons pink peppercorns (optional)\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The marinated goat cheese can be kept refrigerated for up to 1 week, but not any longer than that (infused olive oil can run the risk of botulism if kept for longer than 1 week, even if refrigerated).",
